  "title": "Empowering Ohio's Seniors: Exploring the PASSPORT Waiver",
  "summary": "If you live in Ohio, you might have heard of the Ohio PASSPORT Waiver. PASSPORT is an acronym that stands for Preadmission Screening System Providing Options and Resources Today. It is a Medicaid Waiver that helps older Ohioans live independently in their own homes for longer by providing options for long-term care services and support.",
